-`colour_λ · (λ₀/λ)²` as a `float4[6]` array (rgb + `λ₀/λ`).
+**The LOD is what makes the deposit an integral rather than a lottery.** `u = r · fScale / s_q`,
+so one pixel of `r` is `f = fScale / s_q` texels of `u`; reading level `log₂ f` returns the mean
+intensity over the pixel's own footprint in one tap, and the surviving `1 / s_q²` (the texel
+count in that footprint) turns that mean into the footprint's integral. The energy bookkeeping
+of §2.4 is unchanged — what changes is that the *sampling* now integrates instead of point-
+testing 1 texel in 17. Never go below level 0 (`max(f, 1)`): the pattern can be magnified, in
+which case level 0 is already finer than a pixel.
+
+`kernelLod(u, θ, lod)` samples `$DiffractionKernel` with `SampleLevel` at
+`0.5 + u/L · (cos θ, sin θ)`; `ring(θ)` samples `$DiffractionRing` at `θ / 2π` (bilinear, wrap).
+The kernel's sampler must be **`TrilinearClamp`** — CRYENGINE builds `FILTER_LINEAR` samplers
+with `MaxLOD = 0`, which would silently pin every `SampleLevel` back to level 0 and undo the
+whole chain. Constants: `DiffractionParams0 = (R_sprite_px, s_q, R_tex, norm)`,
+`DiffractionParams1 = (dispersion, L, maxLod = mips − 1, 0)`, and the six
+`colour_λ · (λ₀/λ)²` as a `float4[6]` array (rgb + `λ₀/λ`). The debug view
